@@section 1
@@title CQ-TT American spelling in own lang text, 2026-11-17 ([tooltips.md](../tooltips.md); [plan_rules_fixes.md](../plan_rules_fixes.md) section 15b, TODO `conventions #32`)
@@date 2026-11-17
@@reviewed 2026-11-17
@@jars creativelabels creativedelight creativecompat
@@sources development/creativeLabels/src/main/resources/assets/creativelabels/lang/en_us.json development/creativeDelight/src/main/resources/assets/creativedelight/lang/en_us.json development/creativeCompat/src/main/resources/assets/creativecompat/lang/en_us.json
@@text
@@text Needs the Labels, Delight and Compat jars rebuilt after 2026-11-17 (the lang values changed in source only; P5 rebuilds every jar).
@@table
## CQ-TT-01 | Label and Eraser tooltips use "color" and "labeled"
@group client
@commands Served client (`qrun.py client`): read the Label and Eraser tooltips with shift held
@pass Label: "Right-click with a dye: color the icon"; Eraser: "Right-click a labeled item in your inventory: remove its last label"; no "colour" or "labelled" line
@fails creativelabels jar older than the lang edit (rebuild `:creativeLabels:`)
do {"tooltip_text": "creativelabels:label", "shift": true, "reject": "colour"}
expect READ tooltip_text creativelabels:label \d+: .*color the icon
do {"tooltip_text": "creativelabels:eraser", "shift": true, "reject": "labelled"}
expect READ tooltip_text creativelabels:eraser \d+: .*Right-click a labeled item
## CQ-TT-02 | Oven heat lines say "fueled"
@group client
@commands Place an Oven on a stone block (no heat), open it: the status line; JEI on any baking recipe: the heat line
@pass Oven screen: "Not heated: needs fire, a lit campfire, lava, magma or a fueled blaze burner below (not a stove)"; JEI baking page: "... or a fueled blaze burner (not a stove)"; no "fuelled" (LOOK)
@fails creativedelight jar older than the lang edit (rebuild `:creativeDelight:`)
@draft no driver step opens a placed block's screen or a JEI category page by name yet; owner LOOK
## CQ-TT-03 | MCA gray eyes option
@group client
@commands MCA villager editor (or the player editor) with Creative Compat's extra eye colors: the eye color list
@pass the option reads "Gray Eyes", not `Grey Eyes` (LOOK)
@fails creativecompat jar older than the lang edit (rebuild `:creativeCompat:`)
@draft no driver step opens the MCA editor; owner LOOK

@@section 2
@@title CQ-TT Palette test item switch, 2026-11-17 ([tooltips.md](../tooltips.md) TT-45; [plan_rules_fixes.md](../plan_rules_fixes.md) section 9, V-45, TODO `conventions #20`)
@@date 2026-11-17
@@reviewed 2026-11-17
@@jars creativecommon
@@sources development/creativeCommon/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/creativecommon/CommonConfig.java kubejs/client_scripts/tooltips.js
@@text
@@text `[tooltips] paletteDemo` in `creativecommon-common.toml` (default false; the owner's config sets true until TODO `tooling/design-rules #4`). Read when the client scripts load, so each value needs its own client boot. Needs the Creative Common jar of 2026-11-17 or later.
@@table
## CQ-TT-04 | paletteDemo = true: White Wool and White Concrete show the palette
@group client
@commands Client booted with `paletteDemo = true` (`qrun.py toml config/creativecommon-common.toml tooltips paletteDemo true` on the client instance before boot); read the White Wool and White Concrete tooltips
@pass White Wool: Normal, Uncommon, Rare, Epic, Legendary, Good, Warning, Engineering lines; White Concrete: Black to White, 16 lines
@fails Common older than the key (the script reads false), or the key missing from the client's config file
do {"tooltip_text": "minecraft:white_wool"}
expect READ tooltip_text minecraft:white_wool \d+: .*Legendary
do {"tooltip_text": "minecraft:white_concrete"}
expect READ tooltip_text minecraft:white_concrete \d+: .*Light Purple
## CQ-TT-05 | paletteDemo = false: no palette lines
@group client
@commands Client booted with `paletteDemo = false` (`qrun.py toml config/creativecommon-common.toml tooltips paletteDemo false` before boot); read the same two tooltips
@pass no Normal to Engineering lines on White Wool, no color-name lines on White Concrete; `logs/kubejs/client.log` has no `[NCH.cfg] no creativecommon:TOOLTIPS` warning
@fails the script ignores the key (tooltips.js), or the section is not found (CommonConfig.TOOLTIPS)
do {"tooltip_text": "minecraft:white_wool", "reject": "Legendary"}
do {"tooltip_text": "minecraft:white_concrete", "reject": "Light Purple"}
kjsreject \[NCH\.cfg\] no creativecommon:TOOLTIPS

## CQ-TT-06 | Copycat Framed Block pack on: framed blocks show their Framed Blocks names
@group client
@commands Resource pack `Copycat Framed Block` enabled (it is in the pack's default list); F3+T; hover a Framed Slab, a Framed Chest and the Framed Hammer in JEI; place a Framed Chest and open it
@pass names read Framed Slab, Framed Chest, Framed Hammer (no "Copycat" in any framed name or the chest title); the framed blocks still wear the Copycat textures
@fails `resourcepacks/Copycat Framed Block.zip` still holds `assets/framedblocks/lang/en_us.json` (TODO `blocks/framed-and-decor #2`, D4), or another pack in the list renames them
@draft JEI hover and a GUI title by hand
@reviewed 2026-11-22
look the three names and the chest title as the pass says; textures unchanged
